TITLE: Tool Design: Parameter Schema Best Practice
DESCRIPTION: Example of defining a tool's parameter schema using Zod, including clear descriptions for each parameter to aid agent usage. It demonstrates self-documenting parameters with types and examples.

SOURCE: https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/main/docs/src/content/ja/docs/agents/adding-tools.mdx#_snippet_9

LANGUAGE: typescript
CODE:
```
inputSchema: z.object({
  query: z.string().describe("The search query to find relevant information"),
  limit: z.number().describe(
    "Number of results to return. Higher values provide more context, lower values focus on best matches"
  ),
  options: z.string().describe(
    "Optional configuration. Example: '{'filter': 'category=news'}'"
  ),
}),
```

