TITLE: Agent Constructor and Parameters
DESCRIPTION: Defines the constructor for the Agent class, detailing its configuration parameters for creating an AI agent, including its name, instructions, model, tools, and optional settings.

SOURCE: https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/main/docs/src/content/en/reference/agents/agent.mdx#_snippet_1

LANGUAGE: APIDOC
CODE:
```
Agent Constructor:
  constructor(config: AgentConfig<TAgentId, TTools, TMetrics>)
    Initializes a new instance of the Agent class.

    Parameters:
      config: An object containing the configuration for the agent.
        - name: string (required) - Unique identifier for the agent.
        - description: string (optional) - An optional description of the agent's purpose and capabilities.
        - instructions: string | ({ runtimeContext: RuntimeContext }) => string | Promise<string> (required) - Instructions that guide the agent's behavior. Can be a static string or a function that returns a string.
        - model: MastraLanguageModel | ({ runtimeContext: RuntimeContext }) => MastraLanguageModel | Promise<MastraLanguageModel> (required) - The language model to use for generating responses. Can be a model instance or a function that returns a model.
        - tools: ToolsInput | ({ runtimeContext: RuntimeContext }) => ToolsInput | Promise<ToolsInput> (optional) - Tools that the agent can use. Can be a static object or a function that returns tools.
        - defaultGenerateOptions: AgentGenerateOptions (optional) - Default options to use when calling generate().
        - defaultStreamOptions: AgentStreamOptions (optional) - Default options to use when calling stream().
        - workflows: Record<string, NewWorkflow> | ({ runtimeContext: RuntimeContext }) => Record<string, NewWorkflow> | Promise<Record<string, NewWorkflow>> (optional) - Workflows that the agent can execute. Can be a static object or a function that returns workflows.
        - evals: Record<string, Metric> (optional) - Evaluation metrics for assessing agent performance.
        - memory: MastraMemory | ({ runtimeContext: RuntimeContext }) => MastraMemory | Promise<MastraMemory> (optional) - Memory system for the agent to store and retrieve information. Can be a static memory instance or a function that returns a memory instance based on runtime context.
        - voice: CompositeVoice (optional) - Voice capabilities for speech-to-text and text-to-speech functionality.
```

