TITLE: Agent Initialization with Evals
DESCRIPTION: Demonstrates initializing an AI agent with specific evaluation metrics using the Mastra core library. It imports necessary components for agent creation, OpenAI integration, and various NLP/LLM evaluation metrics like Summarization, Content Similarity, and Tone Consistency. The agent is configured with a model and a set of evals to enable automated quality assessment of its outputs.

SOURCE: https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/main/docs/src/content/en/docs/evals/overview.mdx#_snippet_0

LANGUAGE: typescript
CODE:
```
import { Agent } from "@mastra/core/agent";
import { openai } from "@ai-sdk/openai";
import { SummarizationMetric } from "@mastra/evals/llm";
import {
  ContentSimilarityMetric,
  ToneConsistencyMetric,
} from "@mastra/evals/nlp";

const model = openai("gpt-4o");

export const myAgent = new Agent({
  name: "ContentWriter",
  instructions: "You are a content writer that creates accurate summaries",
  model,
  evals: {
    summarization: new SummarizationMetric(model),
    contentSimilarity: new ContentSimilarityMetric(),
    tone: new ToneConsistencyMetric(),
  },
});
```

