TITLE: Integrate Agents as Workflow Steps
DESCRIPTION: Explains how to use Mastra agents directly as steps within a workflow by creating a step from an agent instance using `createStep(agent)`.

SOURCE: https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/main/packages/core/src/workflows/README.md#_snippet_24

LANGUAGE: typescript
CODE:
```
// Agent defined elsewhere
const myAgent = new Agent({
  name: 'myAgent',
  instructions: '...',
  model: openai('gpt-4'),
});

// Create Mastra instance with agent
const mastra = new Mastra({
  agents: {
    myAgent,
  },
  vnext_workflows: {
    myWorkflow,
  },
});

// Use agent in workflow
myWorkflow
  .then(preparationStep)
  .map({
    prompt: {
      step: preparationStep,
      path: 'formattedPrompt',
    },
  })
  .then(createStep(myAgent)) // Use agent directly as a step
  .then(processResultStep)
  .commit();
```

